From f4bf67d6ff8df80cc144ca63a326471b7f09af4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vips9711 <vips9711@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:38:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Wallet Edition: fix first-run integration-test failures
 (cloud box)

Triaged the 7 failing service test tasks from the first full IT run on the cloud
build box (local HW can't run them). Real fixes:
- commission-service: CommissionProperties is a record; WE-PRICE-1's extra
  convenience constructor made the @ConfigurationProperties binding constructor
  ambiguous ("No default constructor found" at context load). Removed it; updated
  its two test call sites to the canonical 5-arg form.
- reconciliation-service: recon_exception and recon_safeguarding_run referenced
  each other with enforced FKs (circular), so Flyway V001__init.sql failed
  ("relation recon_safeguarding_run does not exist"). Softened the
  recon_exception -> run side to a ref= (no enforced FK) to break the cycle.
- workflow-service: registered the new wallet_txn_correction approval resource
  type (WE-OPS-1) to its owner case-management-service in approval-owners.
- tenant-service StarterPackFlowIT: updated GENERIC-pack count assertions that
  grew with intended Wave-2 seed additions (steps 13->14, awaiting_approval 6->10).

Also adds docs/BACKOFFICE_MOVILRED_PLAN.md (MovilRed Admin FSD parity plan).
Remaining 3 failures (fraud ML canary NPE, card-auth JIT timing, sanctions
latency) are environment/perf-sensitive ITs unrelated to Wave 2.

